// endpoint_open_tabs.proto — OpenTabs. HOST section.
//
// THE EDITOR ASKS, THE DAEMON OPENS, THE EDITOR SHOWS. Emacs never shows a
// workspace's tab until the daemon says everything the workspace needs is
// loaded: its session is served by agent-repl's services (daemon, shim,
// store, sidecar) and its web page has drawn its conversation. Emacs asks for
// the workspaces it wants open with this call, loads each visible
// workspace's page at the same moment (the page reports itself drawn with
// ReportPageDrawn), and shows each tab when its `opened` frame arrives, at its
// place in the registry's tab order, never waiting on any other workspace.
//
// The same call serves every open: the editor's startup (every registered
// open workspace at once), and any later one (a workspace created, reopened,
// unhidden, or whose repository section was expanded).
//
// ONLY VISIBLE WORKSPACES ARE BROUGHT UP. A workspace the user hid, or whose
// repository section is collapsed, is answered `opened` at once with its
// `hidden` arm and nothing is started for it; its session starts when it is
// shown again, which the editor asks for with another OpenTabs.
//
// Every step of every workspace's open is a typed frame on this stream, so the
// editor reports progress as one minibuffer line per step.

